@{
    Layout = Context.Request.Query["print"] == "1" ? null : "_Layout";
}
@if (Context.Request.Query["print"] == "1")
{
    <style>
        .sheet {
            padding: 20px;
            font-family: Arial;
        }

        .section {
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }

        .section-title {
            font-weight: bold;
        }

        .schedule-table {
            width: 100%;
            border-collapse: collapse;
        }

            .schedule-table th, .schedule-table td {
                border: 1px solid #000;
                padding: 5px;
            }
    </style>
}

<div class="spec-section">
    <div class="spec-title">Shipment:</div>
    <div class="spec-content">
        <div>
            Seller shall ship the goods within a reasonable time after completion.
            Shipment dates are estimated and not guaranteed.
            Seller may ship earlier or later than the designated date, by any mode, and in full or partial shipments without penalty.
            Each shipment constitutes a separate sale, and Purchaser must pay for units shipped even if partial.
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="spec-section">
    <div class="spec-title">Delivery Acceptance:</div>
    <div class="spec-content">
        <div>
            If Purchaser fails to accept delivery or does not provide required instructions or documents:
            (i) risk of loss passes to Purchaser,
            (ii) goods are deemed delivered, and
            (iii) Seller may store the goods, with Purchaser responsible for all related costs including storage and insurance.
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="spec-section">
    <div class="spec-title">Non‑Delivery:</div>
    <div class="spec-content">
        <div>
            a) The quantity recorded by Seller at dispatch is conclusive unless Purchaser proves otherwise.
        </div>
        <div>
            b) Seller is not liable for non‑delivery unless Purchaser provides written notice within three (3) days of the expected delivery date.
        </div>
        <div>
            c) Seller’s liability for non‑delivery is limited to replacing the goods within a reasonable time or adjusting the invoice to reflect the actual quantity delivered.
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="spec-section">
    <div class="spec-title">Force Majeure:</div>
    <div class="spec-content">
        <div>
            Seller is not liable for failure or delay in manufacturing or shipping due to causes beyond its control,
            including acts of God, war, sabotage, accidents, epidemics, pandemics, labor issues, government restrictions,
            or inability to obtain materials, equipment, or transportation.
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="spec-section">
    <div class="spec-title">Risk of Loss:</div>
    <div class="spec-content">
        <div>
            Unless otherwise stated, goods ship FOB from Seller’s plant in Springfield, Missouri.
            Seller ships to the Delivery Point listed on the Sales Order and is not liable for delays, loss, or damage in transit.
            Purchaser pays all shipping expenses.
            Title passes to Purchaser upon delivery at the Delivery Point.
        </div>

        <div>
            Purchaser grants Seller a purchase‑money security interest in the goods and their proceeds until payment is complete.
            Seller may file financing statements to perfect this interest.
        </div>

        <div>
            If Seller ships using its own trucks, Purchaser bears all risk of loss once goods are tendered at the Delivery Point.
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

